  "capability": {
    "contract_and_behavior": [
      "Core and IR ArtifactID boundaries normalize native str payloads before subclass-overridable string operations can falsify canonical ID text, preserving established non-string callback behavior and malformed-input refusal.",
      "IR artifact-ref normalization preserves all supplied Mapping/model_dump keys for strict InputRef validation; malformed dataclass metadata or supplied fields absent from the persisted projection refuse instead of becoming legacy absence.",
      "PassContext.require_as checks consumed runtime values; lineage validates IDs/task bindings, needs only callable get_manifest for explicit-ID analysis, and leaves iter_artifact_ids optional when IDs are supplied."
    ],
    "chain": "Existing Core CAS/manifest reader and IR artifact-ref, lineage, and pass consumers; no new authority producer or external claim.",
    "surface": "No module-level facade export or DTO schema change is present. Python-visible surface changes: PassContext.require_as is a new member on an exported class, build_artifact_lineage_graph uses a narrow structural reader annotation, and documented normalize_artifact_ref now rejects malformed selectors. Public-surface inventory review remains pending. Full E02 Runtime/Search/GP and installed-package consumers are outside this slice.",
    "semantic_controls": [
      "Hostile str subclass dispatch cannot change normalized prefix/text; derived-prefix and non-string callback observability/refusal controls remain.",
      "Mapping items() omission, model_dump omission, duplicate/non-string keys, and enumerated key without a value are refused through one strict normalization seam.",
      "Actual dataclass instance vs class marker/faux metadata, ClassVar/InitVar, metadata coherence, unknown public fields, inheritance, and slots have explicit controls.",
      "Existing selected CAS identity/tenant and foreign Core/IR ArtifactID serialization controls remain in the 54-test composed run.",
      "Typed pass values and malformed falsey root inputs refuse; valid empty roots preserve fallback; explicit roots change lineage output and optional enumeration remains optional."
    ]
  },
